<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 15 April, from 1191 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1191">1191 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">835 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VI is crowned Holy Roman Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry VI of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen dynasty</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> since 1169, was crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>. Through his wife Constance he won the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in 1194.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-vi-holy-roman-emperor">Henry VI, Holy Roman Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperator-romanorum">Imperator Romanorum</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1277">1277 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">749 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baybars defeats the Mongols at the Battle of Elbistan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> marched from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> into the Mongol-dominated Seljuk Sultanate of Rûm and defeated the Mongol occupation force at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbistan">Elbistan</a>. The victory limited Mongol influence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> and led to open hostilities with the Mongol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1450">1450 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">576 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French victory at Formigny seals the loss of English Normandy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> and cavalry destroyed an English relief army at Formigny. Normandy fell within months; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a> itself ended after Castillon in 1453.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1632">1632 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">394 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gustavus Adolphus defeats Tilly at the Battle of Rain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Rain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, a Swedish army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a> force of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-tserclaes-count-of-tilly">Johann Tserclaes, Count of Tilly</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>. Tilly later died of wounds received in the battle.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-tserclaes-count-of-tilly">Count of Tilly</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1755">1755 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">271 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Samuel Johnson publishes his Dictionary</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-johnson">Samuel Johnson</a>'s Dictionary of the English Language appeared after nine years' work, defining some 42,000 words with literary quotations. It remained the leading English dictionary for over a century.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1817">1817 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">209 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First American school for the deaf opens in Hartford</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thomas Hopkins Gallaudet and the French deaf teacher Laurent Clerc opened what is now the American School for the Deaf in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a>. Its signing community helped give rise to American Sign Language.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1865">1865 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abraham Lincoln dies of his wound</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lincoln died at 7.22 am in a boarding house opposite Ford's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a>. Andrew Johnson was sworn in as president hours later, inheriting the task of Reconstruction.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1912">1912 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Titanic sinks with the loss of more than 1,500 lives</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The liner went down at 2.20 am with lifeboat places for barely half of the 2,224 aboard. The disaster led to the first International Convention for the Safety of Life at Sea in 1914.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fatal crush at Hillsborough stadium in Sheffield</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A crush on the terraces at an FA Cup semi-final killed 97 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liverpool">Liverpool</a> supporters. Fresh inquests in 2016 found they were unlawfully killed and that fans bore no blame.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 15 April <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/guru-nanak"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Guru Nanak</span><span class="tp">1469–1539</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leonhard-euler"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leonhard-euler.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leonhard Euler</span><span class="tp">1707–1783</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kim-il-sung"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kim-il-sung.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kim Il Sung</span><span class="tp">1912–1994</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vigdis-finnbogadottir"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vigdis-finnbogadottir.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vigdís Finnbogadóttir</span><span class="tp">b. 1930</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
